  },
  {
   "index": 29,
   "tag": "blockquote",
   "landmarks": [
    "main"
   ],
   "textLength": 220,
   "text": "Years later he added –\nI wrote ‘Blowin’ in the Wind' in 10 minutes, just put words to an old spiritual, probably something I learned from Carter Family records. That’s the folk tradition. You use what’s been handed down.",
